      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BALLGOWN BANSHEE (8) is a filly by Be Happy Mach  having her first start. Won a trial earlier this week at Bathurst over 1730m. With even luck from the back row she could kick off with a win. COMPLIMENTRY DRINK (2) was out of the money two starts ago then things went amiss last start when she broke and finished a distant last over 1730m at Bathurst. Has the benefit of a good draw. Only needs to get things right to be in contention. SURPRISE ARRIVAL (1) finished eighth at Menangle two starts back then was highly competitive at her latest appearance over 1720m at Young, beaten only 2 metres into second after being close to the pace throughout. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Must raise the bar but a win is not out of the question. OUR REAL REASON (6) faces the starter for the first time. By For A Reason and hails from the John O'Shea stable. Has strong trial form coming into this. Will be right there at the business end.",
